# The build context is the solution root for both images. An allowlist: everything is out
# (so a new top-level folder, a stray file or a secret never reaches a build by accident)
# and only what the two Dockerfiles COPY comes back in. A file a Dockerfile starts to COPY
# is added to the list in the same change.
*

!global.json
!Directory.Build.props
!Directory.Packages.props
!.editorconfig
!Suwageval.Agent/
!Suwageval.Contracts/
!Suwageval.Server/
!Suwageval.Web/

# Inside the allowed folders: build output and caches of the host.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/

# The web image only builds the app (tsc over tsconfig.app.json, which leaves e2e tests out, and vite):
# browser tests, their config and their output are not needed.
Suwageval.Web/e2e/
**/*.e2e.ts
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/.vite/
**/coverage/

# Secrets never enter a build context, let alone an image layer.
**/.env
.secrets/
